    {
      "id": "b643043050353b80f77567362b8fe51250221d2a",
      "short_id": "b6430430",
      "created_at": "2025-04-02T13:36:14.000-04:00",
      "parent_ids": [
        "54fac0c60d72bbf01df0aeacd2236bd1c97f0ad5"
      ],
      "title": "expert: Ensure more severe ei is displayed in expert column",
      "message": "expert: Ensure more severe ei is displayed in expert column\n\nThe original solution to #7733 (commit 586df977d1e616e0768b99f0581)\ntries to set the value of COL_EXPERT if the newly added expert info's\nseverity is greater than (or equal to) its item or that of any of its\ndescendants. Because items can be faked (and often are when dissecting\nthe columns), it also always set the column when expert items were\nadded to faked items.\n\nWhat we really want to do for the column is, as described, have the\nhighest severity of any item in the entire frame. Since items can\nbe faked, but in expert_set_info_vformat we always have the packet info\nstruct at this point, store the highest expert severity in the packet\ninfo struct and use it.\n\nFix #20465\n",
      "author_name": "John Thacker",
      "author_email": "johnthacker@gmail.com",
      "authored_date": "2025-04-02T09:25:49.000-04:00",
      "committer_name": "John Thacker",
      "committer_email": "johnthacker@gmail.com",
      "committed_date": "2025-04-02T13:36:14.000-04:00",
